.Dd October 1, 2026
.Dt QCOM_ADSP 4 aarch64
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm qcom_adsp
.Nd "Qualcomm audio and compute DSP loader"
.Sh SYNOPSIS
To compile this driver into the kernel,
place the following lines in your
kernel configuration file:
.Bd -ragged -offset indent
.Cd "device qcom_scm"
.Cd "device qcom_adsp"
.Ed
.Pp
Alternatively, to load the driver as a
module at boot time, place the following line in
.Xr loader.conf 5 :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
qcom_adsp_load="YES"
.Ed
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
driver starts the audio DSP (ADSP) and the compute DSP (CDSP, which holds
the NPU) of Qualcomm Snapdragon systems-on-chip with their board's
firmware.
It loads each DSP's firmware into the memory reserved for it, and has the
TrustZone firmware authenticate it and start the DSP through
.Xr qcom_scm 4 .
Before a DSP that needs them starts, it votes, through
.Xr qcom_rpmh 4 ,
the DSP's power rail to its highest level and its path to memory to its
highest bandwidth, as Linux holds them while the DSP boots; the votes
stay.
The firmware is read once the root file system is mounted, from a
.Xr firmware 9
module named after the file's path in linux-firmware with
.Ql / ,
.Ql \&.
and
.Ql -
turned into
.Ql _ ,
or from
.Pa /boot/firmware .
.Pp
The firmware is specific to each board, which the driver recognizes by its
SMBIOS system maker and product, and each DSP by its ACPI hardware ID.
On the Radxa Dragon Q8B, the ADSP runs Radxa's fan control, which parks the
fan when the system is cool; without the ADSP the fan runs at full speed.
.Pp
The driver does not otherwise communicate with the DSPs, and cannot stop
them: it cannot be detached while a DSP runs.
Once running, they talk to the application processors over
.Xr qcom_glink 4 .
.Sh HARDWARE
The
.Nm
driver attaches to the ACPI devices with hardware IDs
.Qq QCOM061B
(the ADSP) and
.Qq QCOM06B0
(the CDSP) on the following boards:
.Pp
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
Radxa Dragon Q8B (Qualcomm Snapdragon 8cx Gen 3, SC8280XP),
with firmware
.Pa qcom/sc8280xp/radxa/dragon-q8b/qcadsp8280.mbn
for the ADSP and
.Pa qcom/sc8280xp/qccdsp8280.mbn
for the CDSP.
.El
.Sh SYSCTL VARIABLES
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Va dev.qcom_adsp.%d.state
Whether the DSP is waiting to start, starting, running or stopped, or
why it failed to start.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr qcom_glink 4 ,
.Xr qcom_rpmh 4 ,
.Xr qcom_scm 4 ,
.Xr qcom_tsens 4 ,
.Xr firmware 9
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
driver first appeared in
.Fx 16.0 .
.Sh AUTHORS
The
.Nm
